Johar added: &#8220;The love and response to Season 1 reaffirmed that audiences connected deeply with Bae's tumultuous journey and her unapologetic approach to life.

&#8220;With Season 2, we wanted to take that world further, exploring new facets of Bae while retaining the humor, heart, and irreverent spirit that was widely loved. We are excited to reunite with Prime Video to bring viewers a new phase of Bae's life, as she and her beloved behens embark on another chapter filled with laughter, emotion, and plenty of chaos.&#8221;

David Fincher , Brad Pitt and Quentin Tarantino &#8216;s long-awaited &#8220;Once Upon a Time in Hollywood&#8221; sequel movie, officially titled &#8220; The Further Mis-Adventures of Cliff Booth ,&#8221; has been unveiled to members of the film press, who are calling the Netflix-backed tentpole a &#8220;wildly entertaining&#8221; &#8220;hangout movie&#8221; that is already one of the year's best.

&#8220;David Fincher's The Further Mis-Adventures of #CliffBooth pops, throbs and crackles,&#8221; wrote film critic Simon Thompson. &#8220;Like Once Upon a Time&#x2026; this is a love letter to LA. An eclectic, ragtag cast make this a slick and sexy romp. A salty and slower-burning side piece to Tarantino's original with a fire final act.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Microsoft Apologizes for Massive Outlook Outage, Affected Customers Can Request Credits for Service Interruption Microsoft Says 'No Evidence of Malicious Activity' in Global Outage of Outlook and Exchange Email as It Begins to Restore Services

Tomatometer critic Zach Pope called the film &#8220;a PURE cinematic trifecta of Tarantino's signature chaos, Fincher's meticulous attention to detail, and Brad Pitt's effortlessly charismatic Cliff Booth.&#8221;

He continued: &#8220;All wrapped into a stylish love letter to 1970s Hollywood cinema that reminds us sometimes all you need is a laid-back, wildly entertaining misadventure with a character you just LOVE spending time with. That just might turn into insanity. It's cool, chaotic, charming, and never tries to be more than it needs to be. If you loved Once Upon a Time in Hollywood, this one's absolutely for you. Just as it was for me.&#8221;

The Wrap's Senior Film Reporter Drew Taylor &#8220;absolutely loved&#8221; the film. &#8220;Tarantino and Fincher are like peanut butter and chocolate (the peanut butter is profane and the chocolate dipped in blood). Stop watching anything, go see it on the biggest screen around, have the time of your life. An absolute triumph. The best,&#8221; he wrote . blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

&#8220;The Further Mis-Adventures of Cliff Booth is an absolute banger,&#8221; wrote Critics Choice member Ricky V&#xE1;lero. &#8220;An aesthetically rich film that beautifully captures the relationship between Los Angeles and the movies. Brad Pitt is as charismatic as ever. Truly one of the year's best films.&#8221;

Variety's Clayton Davis described the film as a &#8220;wild, hilarious hangout movie.&#8221; &#8220;Brad Pitt slides back into his beloved Oscar-winning role and gives his best performance since "Once Upon a Time in&#8230;Hollywood." Elizabeth Debicki brings an intoxicating sensuality, and Scott Caan and Peter Weller are such a treat that they could have had triple the screen time,&#8221; he continued. &#8220;The cinematography is gorgeous. If the 2019 film was a love letter to L.A., this one is a full-on sonnet.

&#8220;The Further Mis-Adventures of Cliff Booth&#8221; features the return of Pitt as the eponymous stuntman. The movie is set in 1977, eight years after the events of &#8220;Once Upon a Time in Hollywood,&#8221; and follows Cliff as a Hollywood studio fixer who gets in way over his head while working for a popular movie actor. The supporting cast includes Brad Pitt, Elizabeth Debicki, Scott Caan, Yahya Abdul-Mateen II, Carla Gugino and Peter Weller, among others.

Pitt won the Oscar for best supporting actor for playing Cliff Booth in &#8220;Once Upon a Time in Hollywood,&#8221; which Sony released in theaters in June 2019. The movie was acclaimed and earned a strong $410 million at the worldwide box office. &#8220;Hollywood&#8221; went on to earn 10 Oscar nominations, including best picture and best director.

&#8220;The Further Mis-Adventures of Cliff Booth&#8221; features a screenplay by Tarantino, who opted not to direct the movie because, per his retirement plan, he only plans on directing one more feature film before he leaves the director's chair for good. The first draft of the sequel script clocked in at a whopping 230 pages, Fincher revealed to Empire magazine last month. The director cut 60 pages.

&#8220;The Further Mis-Adventures of Cliff Booth&#8221; opens exclusively in Imax theaters on Nov. 25 and will be available to stream on Netflix starting Dec. 23. Check out first reactions below:

The Estonian film industry may be small but has big ambitions. And there is more that the Baltic country's institutions can and must do to make the sector more sustainable as it balances big foreign productions visiting and local work. Those were key messages of an event at the 25th edition of the Industry@Tallinn & Baltic Event (ITBE) market, part of the 30th edition of the Tallinn Black Nights Film Festival (P&#xD6;FF).

Lennart Mathias M&#xE4;nnik and K&#xE4;tlin Palm presented findings from their master's theses. Among the data findings was that 74 Estonian films screened in the nation's cinemas in 2025. &#8220;It's not all new films. It's films in general,&#8221; M&#xE4;nnik shared. &#8220;And looking at our market and looking at our country size, it's quite an achievement.&#8221; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4],[300,251]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Movies Dual Oscar Winner Christopher Hampton Calls Glenn Close Honorary Oscar "the Least They Can Do," Says AI Is Just "a Super Google" Music IVE, BINI, KiiiKiii, SB19, LiSA and Babymetal Score Grammy Nominations in New Asian Pop Category

Admissions for Estonian films last year hit 334,471, making the domestic share of cinema admissions in Estonia account for 14 percent. The by far biggest public funding support came from the Estonian Film Institute at &#x20AC;10.9 million ($12.0 million), followed by the Cultural Endowment at &#x20AC;3.1 million ($3.4 million) and &#x20AC;1.7 million ($1.9 million).

M&#xE4;nnik's conclusion: Estonia has &#8220;a small domestic market, but a visible national cinema with an audience.&#8221; But he summarized what he sees as key for the future outlook this way: &#8220;building a stronger, more sustainable Estonian film industry.&#8221;

Two key areas that need to be addressed: &#8220;underfunding limits production and creative freedom is under pressure&#8221; due to a lack of development resources and &#8220;rigid or unclear support expectations,&#8221; which can lead to creative caution. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[300,250],[300,251],[620,350],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450],[4,4]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Last but not least, foreign projects &#8220;bring both value and tension,&#8221; M&#xE4;nnik highlighted. &#8220;Service productions [from abroad] bring investment, work and expertise but draw on the same limited workforce as domestic films. Without stronger local production capacity, international growth can leave Estonian films more vulnerable.&#8221;

Among the foreign films and series shot in Estonia have been the likes of Paramount+ spy thriller series The Agency and Tenet .

His suggestions for the Estonian sector and its support: adopt a long-term audiovisual strategy, make funding more diverse and stable, and strengthen the whole production ecosystem.

The big cutting-edge film studio complex Ida Hub just opened last month, with the goal of making Estonia's Ida-Viru region a key production hub. But M&#xE4;nnik highlighted: &#8220;Production conditions are only one part of how the ecosystem works.&#8221;

